ects offered in the year 2012 with more than 2 lecture units, as well as the number of enrolled students for those subjects. List the results ordered by the variance of total units in descending order, and for Political Science, by the maximum lecture units in descending order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4527\", \"desc\": \"For each department that is degree-granting and offered at least one subject in the School of Engineering in 2021, provide the department code, department name, department full name, the number of subjects offered, the total number of enrolled students in those subjects, the variance and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the number of enrolled students in subjects offered by that department (considering only subjects with a non-null subject code description), and, for each subject in 2021 offered by these departments in the School of Engineering, list the subject id, subject title, and the number of enrolled students, but only include subjects where the number of enrolled students exceeds the average enrollment for that department in 2021. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2597\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year, what is the description of the academic year, the department name, the average total units for all subjects offered by that department in terms that match that academic year and have a term status indicator of 'P', and the deviation of each department's average total units from the overall average total units for that academic year? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2272\", \"desc\": \"For the Mathematics department, what is the department name, the average of the total units, the range of the total units, the variance of the total units for courses with total units greater than 0, and for each course level, what is the number of unique students and the minimum CIP program code among their courses, considering only degree-granting departments? Additionally, for each course level, what is the average number of lecture units and the maximum number of lab units for Mathematics courses? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1335\", \"desc\": \"List, for each department, either (a) the department's full name, the range and variance of the total units for degree-granting Mathematics department courses offered in the 2008 academic year along with the long course description for each course (with the reason 'Math 2008 Stats'), or (b) the department name, the average and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for subjects offered by that department (considering only subjects with more than 0 total units) where the average total units is greater than the overall average across all departments (with the reason 'High Avg Units'). Show the columns in the following order: department name, total units range, total units variance, average total units, standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of total units, long course description, and reason for inclusion. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1023\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year where the Mathematics department has at least one unique subject with subject enrollment number greater than 10, what are the academic year, academic year description, department name, number of unique subjects, minimum total units offered, variance of total units, and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of total units for subjects offered in the fall term that are not variable units and are offered by the Mathematics department? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2335\", \"desc\": \"For each department name and course level, where the total number of enrolled students in offered subjects is greater than 10, and the department is Mathematics (Course 18), provide the number of unique courses, the minimum total units among those subjects that are degree-granting courses, the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for Mathematics courses (considering only departments that offer more than five courses), and the number of unique subject codes for Mathematics in the SIS_SUBJECT_CODE table. List the department name, course level, number of unique courses, minimum total units, the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of total units, and the number of unique subject codes, in that order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1350\", \"desc\": \"For each department and school, provide the department name, school name, the average, range, and variance of the number of enrolled students in subjects offered by that department, and the total enrolled students, considering only departments that grant degrees and subjects with at least one enrolled student. Additionally, for each school, include a grand total for all departments in that school in the format of (null department name, school name, nulls for statistics, and total enrolled students). For students whose first name is 'Peter' and who are in the Mathematics department, also show their last name, email address, student year, and the minimum department budget code in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by the student's full name, as well as the department full name and department last activity date. The results include all these columns in the following order: department name, school name, average enrolled students, range of enrolled students, variance of enrolled students, total enrolled students, last name, email address, student year, windowed minimum department budget code, department full name, and department last activity date. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4184\", \"desc\": \"For each department, show the offer department name, the number of distinct subjects offered by the department in the academic year 2012, and for each subject that was offered in the term \\\"2012SU\\\", display the subject key, subject title, academic year, term description, subject enrollment number, subject offered summary key, the average subject enrollment number within each subject key group, and the deviation of each subject's enrollment number from the average enrollment number for its subject key group, ordered by offer department name and subject key. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_41\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year, provide the academic year description and calculate the average and variance of the total units for subjects offered in terms that are not the current term, have a term status indicator of 'P', are offered by the Mathematics department, and are full term subjects. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3311\", \"desc\": \"For each course that has more than 0 enrolled students and a material status key of 'U', list the course number, course number description, number of enrolled students, reserve catalog key, and the dense rank over the material status key ordered by material status key, along with the department name, the range, variance, and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units of courses offered by that department (considering only courses offered this year with non-null total units). Present the results ordered by course number and course number description. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1212\", \"desc\": \"For the Mathematics department (Course 18), provide the department name, the average and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for subjects offered by that department (considering only subjects with more than 0 total units and at least 1 enrolled student), the number of graduate students in the department, and the most recent warehouse load date for those students, considering only departments that are degree granting and students whose year is 'G'. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3078\", \"desc\": \"For each subject title and department name where the total units are greater than 3, give the number of offered sections, the minimum number of enrolled students, and the average lab units for those subjects. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}]}}"
