follow `dw_2737` → row-level AVG. Precedent count: **1** (row-level), 2 (group-aggregate, different phrasing).\n\n## 4. Business Usage\n`dw_3868`/`dw_4287` serve \"status-U reserve material + textbook detail\" question patterns; `dw_4527`/`dw_3644`/`dw_1212` serve \"degree-granting department unit/enrollment dispersion\" patterns; `dw_2737` serves \"group-vs-overall 20% classification\" patterns. This question is a composition of all three.\n\n## 5. Coverage Checklist\nInvestigated: `LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL`, `TIP_DETAIL`, `TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED`, `SIS_DEPARTMENT`, `SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY`, `LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR`, `LIBRARY_RESERVE_CATALOG`, `LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED` (via `semantic_get`); metrics `dw_3868`, `dw_4287`, `dw_4527`, `dw_2737`, `dw_2913`, `dw_3131`, `dw_3985`, `dw_2580`, `dw_3311`, `dw_3356`, `dw_3664`, `dw_4683`, `dw_1350`, `dw_3644`, `dw_1212`, `dw_3163`, `dw_2335`, `dw_1766`, `dw_2272` (via `semantic_get`/`semantic_search`). `mysql_query` attempted 12× — all failed with access-denied (infrastructure), so no data-level verification was possible.\n\n## 6. Recommendation\n\n**6a.** Department stats from `SIS_DEPARTMENT ⋈ SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY` (only table with both `TOTAL_UNITS` and `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS` + dept code; 3 precedents). Library block from `LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL ⋈ TIP_DETAIL ⋈ TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED` filtered to status `'U'` (exact `dw_3868`/`dw_4287` precedent). Overall average = row-level `AVG(NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS)` over the same filtered population (`dw_2737` precedent). Join the two blocks on `DEPARTMENT_CODE = OFFER_DEPT_CODE`.\n\n**6b.** Three CTEs (dept stats, overall avg, library materials with window), then `CROSS JOIN` overall and `JOIN` library on dept code. CASE uses `> overall*1.2` / `< overall*0.8` per `dw_2737`. Window computed inside the library CTE before the dept join (precedent behavior). 16 SELECT columns in asked order.\n\n**6c.** *Data*: `SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY` is the sole table with both required measures; `TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED` supplies title/faculty/dept-name as in precedents. *Semantic-network*: documented joins `OFFER_DEPT_CODE↔DEPARTMENT_CODE`, `SUBJECT_ID` link across material programs; `dw_2737` decision pattern for classification. *Business*: question is a literal composition of `dw_3868` + `dw_4527` + `dw_2737` shapes.\n\n**6d.** Tie-breaker note: \"overall average\" could alternatively be the average of departmental averages (`dw_2913`/`dw_3131` style). I follow `dw_2737` (row-level) because the question's phrasing \"the overall average\" matches `dw_2737` exactly and the task tip's exception clause directs following a same-shape row-level precedent. The discriminating fact would be the reference SQL's overall-average definition, which I could not verify due to DB inaccessibility.\n\n",
